.SS "int32_t schultz_window_options::vsync"
Nonzero paces the loop to the display, which is what an application wants\&. Zero presents as fast as the machine allows, which is what measuring wants\&. A zeroed struct means zero, so schultz_window_options_init exists to turn it back on\&. 
.PP
